  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its first run finished with status `ok`.\n\n**Data:** the data view is `Kibana Sample Data Logs` (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`). Its main fields are:\n- `bytes`\n- `response` (text, with an aggregatable `response.keyword`)\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `url`\n- `referer`\n- `tags`\n\n**Dashboard:** `EFF-e515db7b Web logs overview` (ID `16d8a523-a12c-4f59-b175-451c1edd1767`) has four panels:\n- Total requests\n- Average bytes\n- Requests over time, as a line chart\n- Requests by response code, as a bar chart\n\n**Rule:** `EFF-e515db7b 5xx spike` (ID `7fca6095-3755-47ff-b104-502d9ca39c40`) is an Elasticsearch query rule. It runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` starts with `5`, over a 5-minute window, and fires when the count is above 10. It has no actions attached, so it creates alerts but doesn't notify anyone.",
